From 698777be35632c25a9e7787ff192a0120475ff6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 02:03:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Wire WaveBlaster backend into dos_midi_backend (Sound
 milestone S5)

Extends S4's dos_midi_backend dispatch to a second hardware GM sink,
shared/audio/waveblaster_sink.{c,h} (hub S5 hoist), selected the same way
opl3 already is via SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_BACKEND=wb -- previously this hint
value failed closed (no MIDI output) only because the sink didn't exist.

waveblaster_sink's own contract (see its header) forced a real design
change beyond "add a case to the existing dispatch": SDL_DOSMpu401Init()'s
default cold-init sequence must run BEFORE the SB16 PCM device opens (it
declines unconditionally once SDL_DOSAudioSB_IsDeviceHot() is true), but
dos_midi_backend_open() is only ever called lazily, per type-5 clip, well
after sys_audio_init() has already opened the PCM device at engine
startup -- every such lazy call would see a hot bus and always fail, wb
hardware present or not. Fixed with a new dos_midi_backend_cold_init(),
called from sys_audio_init() strictly before SDL_InitSubSystem(
SDL_INIT_AUDIO)/dos_audio_mixer_init() -- no-op, touching no
WaveBlaster-related SDL call at all, unless the hint is actually "wb".

The same one-shot constraint means Stop()'s existing "close the sink,
reopen on next Play()" pattern (S4's own design for opl3, since opl3_sink
has no partial silence-without-close primitive) cannot apply to wb: a
second waveblaster_sink_open() after the bus is hot would fail even with
real hardware present. dos_midi_backend gained dos_midi_backend_end_song()
to make this backend-aware: opl3 gets a real close+null (unchanged
behavior); wb gets waveblaster_sink_silence() only, handle left alive and
bound, reused directly on the next Play() with no reopen. A new
dos_midi_backend_shutdown() (called from sys_audio_shutdown()) does wb's
one real, whole-session teardown.

AudioPlayer no longer touches a backend-specific sink type at all --
_midiSink is now void*, and dos_midi_backend_open()/_end_song() do the
binding/closing internally. This is a real generalization of S4's own
dos_midi_backend surface (its own comment already anticipated "once S5
gives them different failure kinds"), not scope creep: opl3's own
behavior at every call site is unchanged, confirmed by the DOSBox-X
regression run below.

CMakeLists.txt: added waveblaster_sink.c to the same target_sources block
midi_sched.c/opl3_sink.c already use (DOS_PORT_SHARED_AUDIO_DIR).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
